This is really an Insightful technical support issue.  My guess is that 
you first started from the account owning splus, and today tried as a user 
account.

We have found that the only successful approach in a multi-user 
environment is to start the license manager from the rc* files: there are 
instructions on how to do so somewhere in the installation instructions. I 
have a file SplusLic containing

#!/bin/sh

#
# Startup for Splus License manager
#

case "$1" in
'start') [ -r /usr/local/bin/Splus ] &&
         /usr/local/bin/Splus LICENSE server start &&
         echo 'Splus LICENSE server start'
         ;;
'stop')   [ -r /usr/local/bin/Splus ] &&
         /usr/local/bin/Splus LICENSE server stop
         ;;
*)
         echo "Usage: SplusLic { start | stop }"
         ;;
esac
exit 0

linked to /etc/rc5.d/S99SplusLic on Fedora Core 3.

