From dimitrios.rizopoulos at student.kuleuven.ac.be  Mon Apr  4 12:58:22 2005
From: dimitrios.rizopoulos at student.kuleuven.ac.be (Dimitris Rizopoulos)
Date: Mon, 04 Apr 2005 14:58:22 +0200
Subject: Re: Q; Matrix manipulation
References: <20050404124413.20124.qmail@web61309.mail.yahoo.com>
Message-ID: <013101c53915$fb776710$0540210a@www.domain>

presuming that each row of your matrix has at least 5 non-missing 
entries, then you could use something likes this:

res <- apply(mat, 1, function(x){
   x <- x[!is.na(x)]
   x <- sort(x)
   out <- if((nx <- length(x)) > 9) mean(x[3:(nx-2)]) else 
mean(x[2:(nx-1)])

   out
})

and then just

cbind(mat, Mean=res)

I hope it helps.

Best,
Dimitris

