A potential wrinkle is the particular integer bit pattern that gets 
interpreted in a special manner by S-PLUS (the integer NA value):

> 2146435073
[1] NA
> 2146435073.0
[1] 2146435073
> 2146435073.0 + (-2:2)
[1] 2146435071 2146435072 2146435073 2146435074 2146435075
> as.integer(2146435073.0 + (-2:2))
[1] 2146435071 2146435072         NA 2146435074 2146435075
> 2146435071
[1] 2146435071
> 2146435071 + 0:4
[1] 2146435071 2146435072         NA 2146435074 2146435075
>

It's not insurmountable, but you do need to be careful how you use and 
pass around the data that is to be interpreted as a word of bits.

-- Tony

