From Horace.Tso at pgn.com  Tue Apr  5 17:10:01 2005
From: Horace.Tso at pgn.com (Horace Tso)
Date: Tue, 05 Apr 2005 10:10:01 -0700
Subject: Summary: bitwise op
Message-ID: <s2526407.082@pgn.com>

I'd like to thank Steven Wofsy for the elegent two-liner function (see below), Bill Venables for pointing out the function expand.grid and that I'm in the real world of finite memory and chip power, Tony Plate for pointing out this quirky feature (bug?) of Splus that 2,146,435,073 is associated with 'NA' (which makes absolutely no sense unless the designers of Splus presume real problems don't involve large numbers), Richard Heiberger for giving out some very useful binary arithmatic routines (shown below), Ray Brownrigg for a recursive version of my loop, Patrick Burns for suggesting the use of '0/1' strings instead of bits.

 

I've always been wary of Splus' inefficient memory usage. However it's hard to resist coding certain very simple combinatoric problems in S precisely because of its coding simplicity. 

 

Horace W. Tso

 

=======================================

 

# Steven Wofsy's suggestion

 maskn<-function(a, n)
{
        tt <- 2.^n
        a %% tt >= tt/2.
}

# In the realm of the infinite RAM and chip speed

# DON'T TRY 

expand.grid(rep(list(0:1), 32))

 

# Followings due to Richard Heiberger

base.0 <- function(x, basis=c(2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2)) {
  cb <- cumprod(c(1,basis))
  xx <- x
  y <- rep(0, length(cb))  
  for (i in length(cb):1) {
    yy <- xx %/% cb[i]
    if (yy > 0) {
      y[i] <- yy
      xx <- xx %% cb[i]
    }
  }
  names(y) <- cb
  y
}

 

baseinv <- function(y, basis=c(2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2)) {
  sum(y * cumprod(c(1,basis)))
}

base <- function(x, basis=c(2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2),
                 trace.steps=F, overflow.truncate=T) {
  cb <- cumprod(c(1,basis))
  xx <- x
  y <- rep(0, length(cb))  
  for (i in length(cb):1) {
    yy <- xx %/% cb[i]
    if (yy > 0) {
      y[i] <- yy
      xx <- xx %% cb[i]
    }
    if (trace.steps) {
      if (i==length(cb)) cat("x", x, "\n")
      cat("xx", xx, "yy", yy, "position", cb[i], ", y", y, "\n")
    }
    if (overflow.truncate && (i==length(cb)) && (y[i] > 1)) {
      y[length(cb)] <- 1
      if (trace.steps)
        cat("xx", xx, "yy", yy, "position", cb[length(cb)], ", y", y, "\n")
    }
  }
  names(y) <- cb
  y
}

 

 

