Subject: Regressing on a distance matrix
Message-ID: <000e01c53aa8$706a0440$67fea8c0@RasmusE>

Dear S-plussers

 

I have an analytical problem for which I would
appreciate your advice. I am running S-Plus 6.1 professional in Windows XP.

 

I have data from a factorial experiment on grassland
succession with 4 2-level treatments (soil type, nutrient level, defoliation
and colonisation sequence) and 10 replicates. My response is the resulting vegetation
composition recorded as the abundance of 48 plant species in each of the 160
experimental units.

 

In order to investigate treatment effects on the
resulting vegetation composition, I have calculated a disimilarity-matrix
including all pairwise comparisons between units. I thus have 12720 inter-unit distances
structured as a data frame with distance in a single column and treatment
differences of each of the 4 main treatments in additional columns. 

 

Is there any appropriate statistical procedure
available to test for the effect of treatment differences on the variation in
inter-unit distance? I have done it with a traditional ANOVA and the result appears
sensible, but obviously I am violating the assumption of independent observations
as well as inflating the residual degrees of freedom. I have been thinking of a
permutation test, but have not been able to find an appropriate S-Plus
functionality. 

 

Regards

   

