Hello, yes sequence will do, but it
actually faster to use

 

getrows<-function(setnum,nparm){1+(0:(setnum-1))*nparm}

 

(setnum is >=1)

While its faster than
seq(from=1,by=nparm,length=setnum) by a factor of 4, its not much of a
difference in real time for small values of setnum.

 

If you can use the “colon”
operator, or bultin type functions, the results are faster.

 

> getrows(3,6)

[1]  1  7 13

> getrows(1,6)

[1] 1

> getrows(6,6)

[1]  1  7 13 19 25 31

 

 

