From tjagger at blarg.net  Thu Apr  7 19:46:22 2005
From: tjagger at blarg.net (Thomas Jagger)
Date: Thu, 07 Apr 2005 13:46:22 -0600
Subject: Re: subscripting
In-Reply-To: <Pine.LNX.4.62.0504071515160.20499@ralph.geog.buffalo.edu>
References: <Pine.LNX.4.62.0504071515160.20499@ralph.geog.buffalo.edu>
Message-ID: <20050407184625.238AB277946@mail.blarg.net>

You might want to try the following

t(cedevec[1:3]/t(aebetestDS[,1:3])) since Splus will try to make a matrix by
filling each column using cedevec[1:3], even if it does not fill correctly.
then dividing. 

For example:

w1<-matrix(1,nrow=5,ncol=3)
> w1
     [,1] [,2] [,3] 
[1,]    1    1    1
[2,]    1    1    1
[3,]    1    1    1
[4,]    1    1    1
[5,]    1    1    1
> w2<-c(1:3)
> w2
[1] 1 2 3
> w2*w1
     [,1] [,2] [,3] 
[1,]    1    3    2
[2,]    2    1    3
[3,]    3    2    1
[4,]    1    3    2
[5,]    2    1    3

but:

> t(w2*t(w1))
     [,1] [,2] [,3] 
[1,]    1    2    3
[2,]    1    2    3
[3,]    1    2    3
[4,]    1    2    3
[5,]    1    2    3
>

does what you want.

