Do you want to replace the median line with the mean?  or add an
additional line/symbol for the mean leaving the median line how it is?

If you want to replace the median line with the mean then you can run
the boxplot function with plot=F and save the output, then replace the
3rd row in the stats matrix with the mean and use the function bxp or
boxes to do the plotting.

If you want to add an additional symbol/line to the complete boxplot,
then run the boxplot as usual, but save the output (the x coords of the
centers of the boxes) and use this along with the means in the points or
segments functions to add your mean.

See the help on boxplot, bxp, and boxes.

