Well, we don't know exactly what you did.  But a Cox model does not have 
an identifiable intercept.

A coxph object has component `linear.predictors' not `lp'.  Is that what 
you mean?   If I recall correctly it is centred at the mean of the 
covariates (that is the linear predictor is taken as zero for an average 
subject).  You can get the log-odds for a pair by differencing their 
linear predictors.

