From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Wed Apr 27 21:09:31 2005
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Wed, 27 Apr 2005 22:09:31 +0100
Subject: Re: comparing two aov models
In-Reply-To: <327C2434A3DA2D4CB61554D644BAE48BAB33EF@LRCPSSMBMXMB001.lrc.ad.gov.on.ca>
References: <327C2434A3DA2D4CB61554D644BAE48BAB33EF@LRCPSSMBMXMB001.lrc.ad.gov.on.ca>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.61.0504272203270.7978@gannet.stats>

You cannot legitimately apply anova() to two models applied to different 
sets of data.  You do have two sets of data, of different sizes.

Cp is Mallow's C_p statistic.  It is not a `test', rather a close relative 
of AIC.  Small Cp is good (and Googling will find you more).  Once again,

it applies to multiple models and one set of data.

